WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.190
In 1990, the world exported
3.46 trillion dollars of goods,

2
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.070
in current prices.

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:13.690
By 2024 it was 24.62 trillion,
and most of it was manufactures.

4
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.070
Now zoom in on one country: Tajikistan.

5
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.850
In 2024, a single inflow of money
equalled almost half of its GDP.

6
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.180
Which flow could be that large,
and does it matter anywhere else?

7
00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:30.290
In this mission, you'll
compare the world's flows:

8
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.630
goods and services, capital,
people and information,

9
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.810
with World Bank and UNCTAD data.

10
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.910
Then you'll choose the
best way to map a flow:

11
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.630
arrows, a Sankey, a chord
diagram, or a choropleth.

12
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.770
Your mission: find out
which flows matter most,

13
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.120
and for which places.
